<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/Vulnerability/7523b8e4bbf5> a airo:Vulnerability ;
    rdfs:label "Disconnect between the AI system's intended emergency function and its actual connection to first responders" ;
    airo:confidenceScore "0.9"^^xsd:float ;
    airo:extractionMode "abstracted" ;
    airo:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d2b158c1fea> ;
    airo:hasSourceDocument <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/document/9513> .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/02975969e9ad> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The robot’s alert button is not yet connected to the police department, said Cosme Lozano, chief of police of Huntington Park, a city just southeast of downtown Los Angeles." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1154" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/03f316efb92c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "California’s First Robotic Police Officer Ignored a Woman Reporting a Crime, Then 'Sang her a Song'" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/183ea92d4837> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[9514] \"HP RoboCop’s capabilities are extremely impressive,\" City Manager Ricardo Reyes said in a statement. [9514] The police department is proud to welcome HP RoboCop as an official member of the police force." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9514" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1f2d2273c493> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2002] The company who designed the bots is called Knightscope. [1154] The Silicon Valley company says it has combined self-driving technology, robotics and artificial intelligence to create what it calls “crime-fighting autonomous data machines.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1154" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/20df325d97aa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1154] The Silicon Valley company says it has combined self-driving technology, robotics and artificial intelligence to create what it calls “crime-fighting autonomous data machines.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1154" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/216d90d95485> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2001] These HP RoboCops, built and leased by Knightscope, are not yet linked up to police departments. [1203] Any help requests are currently sent to a company called Knightscope, which creates and leases the robots." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1203" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/23f42533260a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The PD introduced it in June 2019, saying it would patrol the local park and act as a deterrent to crime." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9511" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/251fcbb94c5d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2001] Cosme Lozano, chief of police at Hungtington Park said, \"That’s why we’re not advertising those features. [9511] Discussing the incident, which resulted in one woman getting beat up, Cosme Lozano, chief of police of Huntington Park, told NBC News that the robot wasn’t yet fully operational, though they didn’t disclose that when they introduced it." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9511" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2909afb306c3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "HP RoboCop stands for Huntington Park RoboCop, the first robotic police “officer” in Huntington Park, California." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9511" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29ad21293f23> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[9513] It turns out that the robot, a K5 model named \"HP RoboCop,\" patrols the park on behalf of the police department [1154] The robot, officially named HP RoboCop, has been patrolling Salt Lake Park for the Huntington Park Police Department since June." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2cb93d312ce6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2001] These HP RoboCops, built and leased by Knightscope, are not yet linked up to police departments. [1203] Any help requests are currently sent to a company called Knightscope, which creates and leases the robots." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1203" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e63292c6daa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[9514] \"HP RoboCop’s capabilities are extremely impressive,\" City Manager Ricardo Reyes said in a statement." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9514" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2fd7ca322a3f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1685] Not all of these droids have been assigned to the police, though. Most act as security guards for gas stations, airports, and businesses. [9511] They’re stated clearly by the company making the robot, a Silicone Valley robotics company called Knightscope, which makes outdoor autonomous robots and has dozens of them in use across the U.S., especially in parking lots, malls and at airports." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/33862ae663e5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2001] Cosme Lozano, chief of police at Hungtington Park said, \"That’s why we’re not advertising those features. [9511] Discussing the incident, which resulted in one woman getting beat up, Cosme Lozano, chief of police of Huntington Park, told NBC News that the robot wasn’t yet fully operational, though they didn’t disclose that when they introduced it." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9511" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/39fd7c2ebc2f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2001] These HP RoboCops, built and leased by Knightscope, are not yet linked up to police departments. [1203] Any help requests are currently sent to a company called Knightscope, which creates and leases the robots." ;
