<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/04115776cf41> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "HP RoboCop, or K5 as Knightscope calls it (they would rather not use the name RoboCop because it creates false expectations in the people interacting with it), may be very smart but it’s not even close to how it should be." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9511" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0596916a4ede> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Back in 2017, an earlier model had a mishap in an office complex in Washington, DC. The Knightscope K5 was making his rounds when he fell into a fountain." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/05a1ad8728cd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The police department is proud to welcome HP RoboCop as an official member of the police force." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9514" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a6b7961f081> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1203] But instead of offering assistance, the egg-shaped robot, whose official name is HP RoboCop, barked at Guebara to ‘Step out of the way’." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1203" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/442fe2a0c6b2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "#MenloPark's SRI International presents the 'Robot for Making Traffic Stops'" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2002" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4f297ea671d7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "California’s First Robotic Police Officer Ignored a Woman Reporting a Crime, Then 'Sang her a Song'" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/55b36b5d92f7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But instead of offering assistance, the egg-shaped robot, whose official name is HP RoboCop, barked at Guebara to ‘Step out of the way’." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1203" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5e13ce2026f2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Californian RoboCop Had To Deal With Its First Crime, And It Did Not Go Well" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9514" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/64e8c1307c22> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police Robot Ignores Woman Trying to Call Police" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/72291673407c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1154] The robot, officially named HP RoboCop, has been patrolling Salt Lake Park for the Huntington Park Police Department since June. [1203] Local Police Chief Cosme Lozano says the robots, which cost between $60,000 and $70,000 a year to lease, are still in a trial phase and that their alert buttons have not yet been activated." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1203" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d2b158c1fea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[9513] Instead, he said, calls go to Knightscope — and will continue to do so until the police department develops protocols for handling calls made through the police bot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d304c2aacd8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "HP RoboCop Shows How Far We Still Have to Go Before AI Could Really Protect Us" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9511" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/86c5cea9326a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police robot told woman to go away after she tried to report crime – then sang a song" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1203" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9c2f289be7e2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "she ran over to a nearby roving LAPD police robot in an attempt to get police dispatched to the area." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2002" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9cb559d2bae3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A mechanical enforcement officer, dubbed HP Robocop, has been patrolling Salt Lake Park, close to Los Angeles, for several months." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1685" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/be5b420731c1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police robot completely ignores woman begging for help" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2002" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bfcfe9c04b0d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The robot, officially named HP RoboCop, has been patrolling Salt Lake Park for the Huntington Park Police Department since June." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1154" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c38a31f558ae> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Cosme Lozano, police chief of Huntington Park, said that the robot’s alert button was not yet hooked up to reach the department, despite it being on ‘patrol’ since June." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2002" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ca6785596329> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[9513] It turns out that the robot, a K5 model named \"HP RoboCop,\" patrols the park on behalf of the police department [9514] The police department is proud to welcome HP RoboCop as an official member of the police force." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9513" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cb394517dac7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A RoboCop, a park and a fight: How expectations about robots are clashing with reality" ;
